---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Local-first. Honest about the signal path.</h2>
      <p>No Electron shell. No telemetry. Just your subscription and a lean native player.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="beats">
      <div class="beat-card">
        <h3>Bit-perfect when the output allows</h3>
        <p>
          Match the device sample rate to the track so nothing is resampled when the
          hardware can do it. TIDE does not take exclusive access of the device —
          other apps can still play sound. Bluetooth and virtual devices stay at their
          own rate because those links re-clock anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="beat-shot">
        <img
          src={`${base}screenshots/bit-perfect.png`}
          alt="TIDE signal path showing bit-perfect playback without exclusive device access"
          width="1200"
          height="900"
        />
      </figure>

      <div class="beat-card">
        <h3>RAM that stays out of the way</h3>
        <p>
          Typically under about 100&nbsp;MB resident while playing, versus
          multi-hundred-megabyte Electron clients. Refresh-rate-first GPU UI without
          shipping a browser.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat-card">
        <h3>I don’t want your data</h3>
        <p>
          Session tokens and library cache live on your Mac. Play counts stay local.
          There is no analytics, crash reporter, or update phoning home — TIDE only
          talks to TIDAL’s own endpoints for music.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
